#N Cyclic spiral seed
#C Eight states laid in a ring around one cell, which is the smallest thing
#C that nucleates a spiral: each state is adjacent to the one that eats it,
#C so the cycle turns rather than settling. Seven cells fill a 64-square grid
#C with spiral arms inside forty generations.
#C Constructed for this library by putting the states in angular order.
x = 3, y = 3, rule = Cyclic CA (8 states)
.AB$G.C$FED!
